    #531 ip30abortkill + #532 stagetokens: four guest-reachable abort() calls, and the gates that reddened because the record got more honest
    
    TWO ROUNDS IN ONE COMMIT, and the entanglement is the reason rather than an excuse: #532's
    checker changes are what make the gate green for #531, and the two rounds share CHANGELOG.md,
    OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md and ledger.json, which cannot be split without interactive staging.
    
    #531 -- dev_sgi_ip30.c: `-E sgi -e ip30' is an advertised machine and a guest LOAD at
    0x0ff10020 zeroed the interrupt-status register and then killed the host.  Three `exit('
    sweeps of this queue walked past every one of these sites, because abort() contains no
    `exit(' -- a census keyed on `exit(' cannot see a host death spelled abort().
    
      * witness: rung 3, unmodified machine, real decode through memory_rw (never `dump' -- all
        four ip30 registrations are DM_DEFAULT, so `dump' bypasses the handler);
      * four abort() calls de-fatalised, live abort() 4 -> 0, exit( 0 -> 0, return 6 -> 6;
      * detector at 33 rows over five kill tables, base 33/33, each PRETABLE block written
        before its table so its mtime proves the order;
      * the repair chain CLOSES: ten cells enumerated, eight killed, two disclosed AND measured,
        zero outside the enumeration.
    
    TWO L4s CORRECTED IN PLACE, both found by the fable5 flagship seat fired last:
      * the disposition table still showed the READ arms as member 3 (DECLINE + LATCHED
        ANNOUNCE) while this round's own F13 ruling had already moved them to member 2 (SILENT
        DECLINE).  Both shipped in one block and a reader meets the table first, so the stale
        half was the load-bearing one.
      * the member-4 correction was HALF a correction: it refuted the LATCH axis and left the
        VALUE axis standing.  heart.h says "WRITE set_isr to set bits"; the code is
        `d->isr = idata' (REPLACE) beside `d->isr &= ~idata' (bitwise) -- one register pair, one
        document, two semantics.  No row can see it because `isr keep' seeds a ZERO ISR, where
        `=' and `|=' coincide.  NOT changed here: `d->isr = idata' is PRE-EXISTING AT HEAD, so
        changing it is a second fix at a second site, and it is already filed as ip30setisrassign.
    
    #532 -- HEAD carried ZERO stage violations; the working tree carried NINETEEN, every one
    created by RECORDING 23 seat answers that already existed on disk.  Recording a seat's remark
    about a row promotes that row's stage from ABSENT (or a one-seat FILING) to a short panel,
    which is what sections H and I redden on.  check_stage_panels.py predicted the class in its
    own comment; it did not predict the scale.
    
      * new token [NOT A PANEL STAGE: NO PANEL CONVENED], because neither existing token was
        TRUE here -- RE_READ says SINGLE-SEAT and these carry 2..8; ANNOTATION asserts a
        pre-2026-08-16 vintage.  The token states the GENERAL claim with the reason in the note,
        deliberately unlike the two above it: a first draft read INCIDENTAL SEAT MENTION, which
        is false of ip30abortkill's assess stage (a witness build and a ship-order ruling).
      * negative-controlled in both directions on BOTH gates before it touched real data, and the
        token entry is proven not to count as a seat -- or marking a gap would close it.
      * TWO MIRRORING BLIND SPOTS, found by asking what the OTHER tools do with a token they do
        not know: check_fable_queue.py never knew RE_READ, and gen_dashboard.py knew none of
        them -- so annotations (conventionally seat: fable5) rendered as FABLE CELLS, asserting
        the flagship had answered stages where no panel was ever convened.  Controlled by render
        diff: the pre-fix generator emits 25,154 more characters, and those are the fabricated
        cells.  One cause for both: a token added where it was needed and never mirrored.
    
    THE SORTING RULE IS THE BRIEF'S SUBJECT, NEVER THE SEAT COUNT.  It overturned the sort three
    times -- asiceventaddr carries a full EIGHT recorded seats and is not a stage (they all cite a
    pass 2 on a comment-only vendored-header commit), while three rows with the same count share
    one dir whose brief IS convened on them.  The flagship seat then overturned it a fourth time,
    ruling panel_20260917_100431 MISDIRECTED for pcc2c040assertrow: the brief named the row and
    inlined only the src/ diff, so the packet-fed seats reviewed a stale comment.
    
    FILED: lcalenzerodrop (HIGH).  #530's CLOSING PASS was recorded with three seats and closed;
    the dir holds five and FOUR dissent.  If the comment's premise "len 0 has no producer" is
    true then `if (len == 0) return 0;' is dead code, so a DROP of it is observationally identical
    to base, scores 352/352, and contradicts the round's claim that no leg scored 352/352.  Filed
    under the late-dissent rule with the dissent carried verbatim; nothing amended under #530's
    number.
    
    The MANIFEST entries naming #529's and #530's uncommitted artefacts are WITHDRAWN from this
    commit and remain as working-tree changes for their own rounds.  Committing #529's
    crime_width_probe.py here would ship a DETECTOR that no COMMITTED gate runs -- HEAD's
    gate_arm.sh does not name it -- under a pin the flagship seat measured wrong (188 vs 204).
    
    Gate: PRECOMMIT_PASS 0 hard, 5 soft.  All four trees two-part clear, no .MUTANT sentinel.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
